    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"The primary objective of this study was to determine if weathering of abandoned mercury mines in Nevada has resulted in any significant effect to surrounding ecosystems. This study is part of a larger U.S. Geological Survey (USGS) project to evaluate the geology, mineral resource potential, and environmental concerns of the Humboldt River Basin, Nevada. Mercury is clearly the primary concern of the mercury mines, but other toxic elements were also evaluated in this study. In this report, we describe the samples collected in 1999 for this study, the methods used for the analysis of the samples, and the geochemical data for these samples.\"",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
